<title>USA: BPA still not offering peak, firm power for Tues.</title>
<headline>BPA still not offering peak, firm power for Tues.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) continued to hold off from offering power during peak hours on Tuesday, the agency said Monday.</p>
<p>For Tuesday, BPA continued to offer power at $7.00 per MWh during hours ending 0100-0600 and 2300-2400 PST to buyers willing to displace thermal generation with hydropower.</p>
<p>Non-firm power during shoulder hours on Tuesday (0700, 1100-1700 and 2100-2200 PST) was unchanged at $9.00 per MWh for Northwest deliveries and $10.00 for COB.</p>
<p>Prices for firm and non-firm power during off-peak hours on Tuesday were unchanged at $9.00 per MWh.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 655 6761))</p>
</text>
